+Cosign Admission Controller — Operator Guide (Hardened Deployment)
+----------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Overview
+- This guide shows steps to provision KMS/HSM keys, configure TLS for the webhook (recommended: cert-manager), deploy the cosign admission Helm chart (helm/cosign-admission), and enforce signature verification in production namespaces.
+
+1) Provision a KMS key (example AWS)
+ - Create key:
+   aws kms create-key --description "cosign key for Aegis" --origin AWS_KMS
+ - Create an alias and grant permissions to the CI service principal to sign:
+   aws kms create-alias --alias-name alias/cosign-aegis --target-key-id <KEY_ID>
+ - Record the key ARN and store in Kubernetes secret:
+   kubectl -n security create secret generic cosign-kms --from-literal=kms_arn=arn:aws:kms:... --dry-run=client -o yaml | kubectl apply -f -
+
+2) Provision TLS for webhook (cert-manager recommended)
+ - Install cert-manager in cluster.
+ - Create Issuer (e.g., ClusterIssuer) for your CA or use ACME if external domain is available.
+ - In Helm values set tls.secretName to the TLS secret that cert-manager will create.
+ - Use the helm chart to deploy; cert-manager will issue certs and populate the secret.
+
+3) Configure CA bundle in ValidatingWebhookConfiguration
+ - After certificate is issued, extract CA bundle and patch the ValidatingWebhookConfiguration caBundle field.
+ - Example:
+   kubectl get secret cosign-webhook-tls -n admission -o jsonpath='{.data.ca\.crt}' | base64 --decode > ca.crt
+   kubectl patch validatingwebhookconfiguration cosign-validating-webhook --type='json' -p='[{"op":"replace","path":"/webhooks/0/clientConfig/caBundle","value":"'"$(base64 -w0 ca.crt)"'"}]'
+
+4) Test signing end-to-end
+ - Sign an example artifact in CI using cosign with KMS key:
+   cosign sign --key $COSIGN_AWS_KMS_KEY_ARN artifact.tar.gz
+ - Try to deploy an image signed with that key into the production namespace; the webhook should allow it. Unsigned images must be rejected.
+
+Notes & Security
+- Use least-privilege IAM roles for signing and verification.
+- Rotate KMS keys periodically; update Helm secret and redeploy webhook accordingly.
+- For HSM: use cloud-specific HSM-backed KMS endpoints that cosign supports.
+
