+# Staged Plan to Move RL Sandbox toward Controlled Automation
+
+Overview
+- RL agent suggests policies in sandbox. This plan describes a staged, risk-controlled path to operator-supervised application, then limited automation.
+
+Stages:
+1) Sandbox & offline evaluation (0-4 weeks)
+ - RL generates candidates; run offline_eval.py on historical traces.
+ - Only candidates with estimated reward > threshold and safety risk = 0 are kept.
+
+2) Human review & manual apply (4-8 weeks)
+ - Human approves top candidates via manual-approval service.
+ - Operator uses safe_apply_operator to apply policy; monitor for 7 days.
+
+3) Canary automation (8-16 weeks)
+ - After 90 days of stable behavior and low safety incidents, allow controller to perform limited automated application for stage_1 percentages (see safe_policy).
+ - Each automated change requires cross-check: acceptance_rate and verifier precision must be within safety margins.
+
+4) Gradual automation (16+ weeks)
+ - Increase automated application windows if metrics remain stable and SMEs sign off.
+ - Maintain human override and audit logs; require periodic re-evaluation.
+
+Controls & Safeguards
+- Manual approval remains required for high-risk channels.
+- All candidate actions are logged in metadata store and evidence saved with Object Lock.
+- Circuit breaker disables RL actions if acceptance_rate < threshold or verifier regressions occur.
+
